{
  "why": [
    "Two implementations of one classifier, held together by a file - the same",
    "arrangement subject_conformance.json uses. The Go CLI shapes a value when",
    "it captures an environment (cli/internal/model/shape.go); the Python",
    "extractor shapes one when it reads a default in code, and the API compares",
    "stored shapes when it diffs two captures (shared/culprit_model/shape.py).",
    "If the two disagreed about what 'the same kind of value' means, the CLI's",
    "diff and the API's diff of the same two captures would report different",
    "things, and neither would error.",
    "",
    "schemes: the Phase 30 scheme classifier (resolving Q7). The scheme is a",
    "closed enum; an unrecognised one is 'other', never the scheme itself.",
    "",
    "equivalence: when two shapes describe the same kind of value. Not struct",
    "equality - length class is compared only as empty-or-not, an unknown type",
    "compares on presence alone, and an unclassified (absent) scheme compares",
    "with anything. Each case says why."
  ],
  "schemes": [
    {"input": "postgresql://orders:hunter2@db.internal:5432/orders", "scheme": "postgresql"},
    {"input": "postgres://db/orders", "scheme": "postgresql"},
    {"input": "postgresql+asyncpg://db/orders", "scheme": "postgresql"},
    {"input": "POSTGRESQL://DB/ORDERS", "scheme": "postgresql"},
    {"input": "mysql+pymysql://db/orders", "scheme": "mysql"},
    {"input": "mongodb+srv://cluster0.example.net/app", "scheme": "mongodb"},
    {"input": "redis://cache:6379/0", "scheme": "redis"},
    {"input": "rediss://cache:6380/0", "scheme": "rediss"},
    {"input": "https://api.example.com/v1", "scheme": "https"},
    {"input": "http://localhost:8000", "scheme": "http"},
    {"input": "amqps://broker/vhost", "scheme": "amqps"},
    {"input": "s3://bucket/key", "scheme": "s3"},
    {"input": "  https://padded.example.com  ", "scheme": "https"},
    {"input": "cockroachdb://db/orders", "scheme": "other"},
    {"input": "hunter2secretvalue://looks-like-a-url", "scheme": "other"},
    {"input": "db.internal:5432", "scheme": "not_applicable"},
    {"input": "8000", "scheme": "not_applicable"},
    {"input": "", "scheme": "not_applicable"},
    {"input": "not a url at all", "scheme": "not_applicable"}
  ],
  "equivalence": [
    {
      "why": "identical shapes",
      "left": {"type": "string", "length_class": "medium", "format": "dsn", "present": true, "scheme": "postgresql"},
      "right": {"type": "string", "length_class": "medium", "format": "dsn", "present": true, "scheme": "postgresql"},
      "equivalent": true
    },
    {
      "why": "two environments' URLs name different hosts, so their lengths differ - that is not a disagreement",
      "left": {"type": "string", "length_class": "medium", "format": "dsn", "present": true, "scheme": "postgresql"},
      "right": {"type": "string", "length_class": "long", "format": "dsn", "present": true, "scheme": "postgresql"},
      "equivalent": true
    },
    {
      "why": "present-but-empty against populated is a real misconfiguration",
      "left": {"type": "string", "length_class": "empty", "format": "not_applicable", "present": true, "scheme": "not_applicable"},
      "right": {"type": "string", "length_class": "short", "format": "opaque", "present": true, "scheme": "not_applicable"},
      "equivalent": false
    },
    {
      "why": "set against unset is the commonest real finding there is",
      "left": {"type": "string", "length_class": "medium", "format": "url", "present": true, "scheme": "https"},
      "right": {"type": "null", "length_class": "not_applicable", "format": "not_applicable", "present": false, "scheme": "not_applicable"},
      "equivalent": false
    },
    {
      "why": "two unset keys agree, whatever else their shapes say",
      "left": {"type": "null", "length_class": "not_applicable", "format": "not_applicable", "present": false, "scheme": "not_applicable"},
      "right": {"type": "null", "length_class": "not_applicable", "format": "not_applicable", "present": false},
      "equivalent": true
    },
    {
      "why": "Q7's own example: the application's postgresql against the environment's mysql",
      "left": {"type": "string", "length_class": "medium", "format": "dsn", "present": true, "scheme": "postgresql"},
      "right": {"type": "string", "length_class": "medium", "format": "dsn", "present": true, "scheme": "mysql"},
      "equivalent": false
    },
    {
      "why": "TLS-or-not is a real difference and is not folded away",
      "left": {"type": "string", "length_class": "medium", "format": "url", "present": true, "scheme": "redis"},
      "right": {"type": "string", "length_class": "medium", "format": "url", "present": true, "scheme": "rediss"},
      "equivalent": false
    },
    {
      "why": "an extractor from before Phase 30 says nothing about schemes, and saying nothing is not disagreeing",
      "left": {"type": "string", "length_class": "medium", "format": "dsn", "present": true},
      "right": {"type": "string", "length_class": "medium", "format": "dsn", "present": true, "scheme": "mysql"},
      "equivalent": true
    },
    {
      "why": "a credential baked into a URL in one environment and not the other is a finding",
      "left": {"type": "string", "length_class": "medium", "format": "dsn", "present": true, "scheme": "postgresql"},
      "right": {"type": "string", "length_class": "medium", "format": "url", "present": true, "scheme": "postgresql"},
      "equivalent": false
    },
    {
      "why": "a number in one environment and a string in the other",
      "left": {"type": "integer", "length_class": "not_applicable", "format": "numeric", "present": true},
      "right": {"type": "string", "length_class": "short", "format": "numeric", "present": true},
      "equivalent": false
    },
    {
      "why": "a set key whose value could not be read disagrees with nothing about its content",
      "left": {"type": "unknown", "length_class": "not_applicable", "format": "not_applicable", "present": true, "scheme": "not_applicable"},
      "right": {"type": "string", "length_class": "medium", "format": "dsn", "present": true, "scheme": "postgresql"},
      "equivalent": true
    },
    {
      "why": "but an unreadable key that is set still disagrees with one that is unset",
      "left": {"type": "unknown", "length_class": "not_applicable", "format": "not_applicable", "present": true},
      "right": {"type": "null", "length_class": "not_applicable", "format": "not_applicable", "present": false},
      "equivalent": false
    }
  ]
}
